-- title:
--   Second special-fibre component's function field from a branch valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the image under coefficientwise extension of scalars $\mathrm{coeffEmb}$ of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $p$ and whose image contains $\zeta$, with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$ (scalar tower $A\to L\to K$), and let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), assumed nonzero. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $c_1:C_1\to\operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2:C_2\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension one and geometrically integral, equipped with closed immersions $i_1,i_2$ over $k$ into the base change to $k$ of the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) of $K$ over $A$ in the coordinate $j$ (that is, morphisms whose composite with the projection $\operatorname{Spec}$-structure map is $c_1$, resp. $c_2$), such that their images jointly cover every point of that base change, the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced with exactly $n$ points for some $n>0$; further given a section $\varepsilon$ of the two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, sections $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ of $c_1,c_2$, the compatibility that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base change of $\varepsilon$, and a datum $w$ consisting of a weight-one modular form for $\Gamma_1(M)$ with an integral $q$-expansion over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose associated constant `intSeriesC` in $k$ is nonzero. The conclusion asserts: for every field $F$ that is a $k$-algebra, every [`AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel k F`](def/AlgebraicCurve_CurveModel.html#L23) (a proper smooth integral curve over $k$ with a specified isomorphism of $F$ onto its function field over $k$, a bijection of its closed points with the places of $F/k$ matching stalks with valuation rings, and finite subsets contained in affine opens) whose underlying scheme is isomorphic to $C_2$ by some $e$ compatible with the structure maps over $k$, there exist a valuation subring $V$ of $K$ containing the image of $A$, with the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ contained in the non-units of $V$, and with $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ both in $V$ for every polynomial $P$ over $A$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal is nonzero, an $A$-algebra structure on $V$ inducing the inclusion $V\subseteq K$, and a minimal prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of $k\otimes_A V$, such that $F$ is isomorphic as a $k$-algebra to $\operatorname{Frac}\big((k\otimes_A V)/\mathfrak{q}\big)$.
--
--   This is the components-to-branches dictionary for the stable reduction of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$: the function field of the second component of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model is realised as the fraction field of a minimal-prime quotient of $k\otimes_A V$ for a valuation subring $V$ of $K$ lying over the maximal ideal of $A$ and over the generic point of the $j$-line in characteristic $p$. It feeds the identification of that function field with the Igusa function field of $X_1$, used in the study of the mod $p$ geometry underlying the level-lowering step.
